# International: language German and keyboard layout German, then OK. 3.1 copies LANGGER.DLL and
# KBDGR.DLL (from A: in arch311-ref/scn/intl-langkbd.scn) and loads them; the port writes the same
# WIN.INI and SYSTEM.INI entries (CONTROL.INI [installed] is the installer's, not written). Run as
# intl.w16 (ARCH311_PRISTINE_INI=1, ARCH311_CLOCK="2026-10-08 09:30:24", applet International).
# regress: ARCH311_PRISTINE_INI=1 ARCH311_CLOCK="2026-10-08 09:30:24" sh tools/run-cp-test.sh "$TEST" "$OUT" International
# compare: intl-langkbd/02.png 01-open.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: intl-langkbd/03.png 02-german.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# ini: WIN.INI intl sLanguage=deu
# ini: SYSTEM.INI boot language.dll=langger.dll
# ini: SYSTEM.INI boot.description language.dll=German
# ini: SYSTEM.INI keyboard keyboard.dll=kbdgr.dll
sleep 900
shot shots/01-open.png
key tab
type g
key tab
type g
sleep 300
shot shots/02-german.png
key enter
sleep 500
quit
